---
import { SalvationVideoPlayer } from "@/components/salvation/salvation-video-player";
import { Prose } from "@/components/starwind/prose";
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/page-layout.astro";
---

<PageLayout
  title="What Does It Mean To Be Saved? | Victory Baptist Church"
  description="The Bible way to heaven — watch a short Plan of Salvation video and learn how to know you have eternal life through Jesus Christ."
>
  <section class="bg-muted px-8 py-14 md:px-16 lg:px-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
      <p
        class="mb-3 text-sm font-semibold tracking-[0.18em] text-primary uppercase"
      >
        The Bible Way to Heaven
      </p>
      <h1
        class="font-display text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-5xl"
      >
        What Does It Mean To Be Saved?
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-muted-foreground">
        Watch this short Plan of Salvation video, then read the Scriptures below.
        God wants you to know that you have eternal life.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-background px-8 py-10 md:px-16 lg:px-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
      <SalvationVideoPlayer client:only="react" />
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        About 55 seconds · Main points of the Gospel with key Bible verses
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-background px-8 pb-16 md:px-16 lg:px-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <Prose>
        <p>Every person eventually asks questions like these:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>What happens after I die?</li>
          <li>Can I know that I will spend eternity with God?</li>
        </ul>

        <p>The Bible says we can know.</p>

        <p>
          In 1 John 5:13, Scripture says, "These things have I written unto you
          that believe on the name of the Son of God; that ye may know that ye
          have eternal life..."
        </p>

        <p>
          God does not want us to live in uncertainty. He wants us to know the
          way of salvation.
        </p>

        <h2>The Problem</h2>

        <h3>Sin separates us from God.</h3>

        <p>
          Before someone can be saved, they must first admit they are lost in
          sin.
        </p>

        <p>
          Romans 3:23 says, "For all have sinned, and come short of the glory of
          God." Since Adam and Eve, sin has affected every person. Sin is
          anything contrary to God's holiness, and our sin separates us from Him.
        </p>

        <p>
          Romans 6:23 says, "For the wages of sin is death; but the gift of God
          is eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord."
        </p>

        <p>
          The penalty for sin is spiritual death and eternal separation from God.
        </p>

        <h3>Good works and religion cannot save us.</h3>

        <p>
          People often try to reach God through religion, effort, or morality.
          But none of those can remove sin.
        </p>

        <p>
          Proverbs 14:12 says, "There is a way which seemeth right unto a man,
          but the end thereof are the ways of death."
        </p>

        <p>
          Ephesians 2:8-9 says, "For by grace are ye saved through faith; and
          that not of yourselves: it is the gift of God: Not of works, lest any
          man should boast."
        </p>

        <p>Salvation is not something we earn. It is a gift God gives.</p>

        <h2>What Has God Done?</h2>

        <h3>Jesus Christ paid the price for our sin.</h3>

        <p>Though we were separated from God, He loved us.</p>

        <p>
          John 3:16 says, "For God so loved the world, that he gave his only
          begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but
          have everlasting life."
        </p>

        <p>
          Jesus died on the cross for our sins and rose again three days later.
          Through His death and resurrection, He paid the debt we could never pay
          ourselves.
        </p>

        <p>
          Romans 5:8 says, "But God commendeth his love toward us, in that, while
          we were yet sinners, Christ died for us."
        </p>

        <h2>How Can I Be Saved?</h2>

        <h3>Trust Jesus Christ alone.</h3>

        <p>
          To be saved, we must stop trusting ourselves, our works, or our
          religion, and place our faith in Jesus Christ alone for forgiveness and
          eternal life.
        </p>

        <p>
          Romans 10:13 says, "For whosoever shall call upon the name of the Lord
          shall be saved."
        </p>

        <p>
          If you are ready to turn to Christ, you can call on Him in faith and
          ask Him to save you.
        </p>

        <p>You may pray something like this:</p>

        <blockquote>
          <p>
            Dear God, I know that I am separated from you because of sin. I
            confess that in my sin, I cannot save myself. Right now, I turn to
            you alone to be my Saviour. I ask you to save me from the penalty of
            my sin, and I trust you to provide eternal life to me.
          </p>
          <p>—Amen</p>
        </blockquote>

        <h2>Do You Have Questions?</h2>

        <p>
          If you would like to talk with someone about salvation or about having
          a relationship with God, please <a href="/visit/">reach out to us</a>.
          We would love to help.
        </p>
      </Prose>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
